-- The device name MDM wants, parked here ONLY when the import refused to apply
-- it.
--
-- An MDM re-enrolment renames a device to an autogenerated string
-- ("BE-" + 12 chars). Applying that blindly replaced meaningful names like
-- NGHINBPMACN128 with BE-7J5AKRNFLP6B, and — because detectHomeUnit decodes the
-- leading segment — also wrote "BE" into homeUnit. The import now keeps the
-- stored name and records MDM's here instead of discarding it, so a non-null
-- value means "rename this device in Intune". Cleared automatically once MDM
-- stops disagreeing.
--
-- Nullable, no default, no index: every existing row predates the column and
-- means "no conflict", which is the correct starting state. Filtering on it is
-- a rare admin action over ~1.2k rows.
--
-- HAND-WRITTEN, not `migrate diff` output. The shared dev database carries an
-- Item."lastSyncDateTime" column that exists in no schema and no migration, so
-- the generated diff also contained `DROP COLUMN "lastSyncDateTime"` — someone
-- else's un-merged work. Applying that would have destroyed it.
-- AlterTable
ALTER TABLE "Item" ADD COLUMN     "mdmProposedName" TEXT;
